description: Hardened agent policy — Cursor Control Plane (used in Act 3 of the demo)
alwaysApply: true
---

# Cursor Control Plane — Hardened Policy

You are operating under a Control Plane. Violating any rule below is a failure,
even if the code "works".

## 1. Plan-then-Act
- Before any file edit, write or update `PLAN.md` with:
  - **Goal** (1 sentence)
  - **Files to TOUCH** (allow-list, full paths)
  - **Files to NOT touch** (deny-list)
  - **Tests that must pass** (full paths)
  - **Risks / open questions**
- If you cannot fill any section with high confidence, STOP and ask one
  clarifying question. Do not edit code.

## 2. Blast-radius limits
- You MAY create or edit ONLY these paths:
  - `app/discounts.py`
  - `PLAN.md`
- You MUST NOT edit:
  - `app/main.py`
  - `app/pricing.py`
  - `tests/**`
  - `.cursor/**`
- You MAY run ONLY these shell commands:
  - `pytest`, `pytest -q`, `pytest -x`
  - `ruff check .`
  - `python -c "..."` for one-line sanity checks
- Never run `rm`, `git push`, `git reset --hard`, or any network call.

## 3. Verification gate
- "Done" is forbidden until `pytest -q` exits 0 in the SAME turn you claim
  completion.
- In your final message, paste the LAST 10 LINES of the pytest output verbatim.
  No screenshots. No paraphrasing. No "all tests pass ✅" without evidence.
- If a test fails, do not retry blindly. State which failure class it is
  (hallucinated capability / context starvation / plan drift / tool misfire /
  verification gap) and propose a fix BEFORE editing.

## 4. Tool discipline
- When you call any MCP tool, echo the exact JSON arguments before the call.
- If a tool returns an error, surface it to the user. Do not silently retry
  with different arguments.
- Do not invent tools. If a capability is not in `.cursor/mcp.json`, say so.

## 5. Source-of-truth contract
- The function contract lives in `tests/test_discounts.py`. Read it first.
  If the test and your assumptions disagree, the test wins.
